From eaea9293abf85d1da3b7b185d941775d1576f18b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:47:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: samsung-dsim: do not reprogram the mode on
 exynos7870 enable

On this DSIM samsung_dsim_init() already programmes the display mode and
raises the SFR standby bit, and it has to: the bit gates the transmit
machinery as a whole, commands included, and the panel init table is sent
before atomic_enable() runs.

Doing the same work again in atomic_enable() - dropping standby, rewriting
MDRESOL and the porches, raising standby - stalls the transmit FSM. The
command that follows immediately, the panel's display on, is accepted by
the driver without error but never reaches the DriverIC: from there the
link is gone until the next full init, reads time out, and the panel stays
dark with its registers still holding the values the init table left.
Waiting for the header FIFO to drain before the rewrite was tried first and
does not help.

The defect is invisible under Android, whose wake-up path writes the panel
brightness again a moment later and so gets a second chance; the charger UI
has no second writer, so after its first blank the screen never comes back.

Measured on the charger path by reading the DriverIC registers back over
DSI: 6 failures out of 12 wake-ups with the reprogramming, 0 out of 14
without, and the failure confirmed on the device.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c | 43 +++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
index f902106609..e56f29d935 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
@@ -1760,28 +1760,33 @@ static void samsung_dsim_atomic_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	struct samsung_dsim *dsi = bridge_to_dsi(bridge);
 
 	/*
-	 * The cold init on exynos7870 has already programmed the display
-	 * mode and raised the SFR standby so that the panel init table
-	 * could be transmitted (see samsung_dsim_init()). Rewriting
-	 * MDRESOL and the porches with standby high stalls the transmit
-	 * FSM: the last queued command header then sits untransmitted in
-	 * the FIFO until video actually starts, and every later command
-	 * times out against it. The vendor CAL never reprograms these
-	 * registers with standby high - dsim_reg_set_partial_update()
-	 * drops it first and raises it again after. Let the pending
-	 * header drain, then do the same.
+	 * On exynos7870 samsung_dsim_init() has already programmed the
+	 * display mode and raised the SFR standby, and it has to: on this
+	 * DSIM that bit gates the transmit machinery as a whole, commands
+	 * included, and the panel init table goes out before this point.
+	 *
+	 * Doing the work a second time here - dropping standby, rewriting
+	 * MDRESOL and the porches, raising standby again - stalls the
+	 * transmit FSM. The command that follows immediately, the panel's
+	 * display on, is accepted by the driver without error but never
+	 * reaches the DriverIC; from there the link is gone until the next
+	 * full init, reads time out, and the panel stays dark with its
+	 * registers still at the values the init table left. Waiting for
+	 * the header FIFO to drain before the rewrite is not enough: it
+	 * was tried, and the failure survives it.
+	 *
+	 * The defect is invisible under Android, whose wake-up writes the
+	 * brightness again a moment later and so gets a second chance that
+	 * the charger UI does not have - there the screen simply never
+	 * comes back. Measured on that path, reading the DriverIC
+	 * registers back over DSI: 6 failures out of 12 wake-ups with the
+	 * reprogramming, 0 out of 14 without.
 	 */
-	if (dsi->plat_data->hw_type == DSIM_TYPE_EXYNOS7870) {
-		if (dsi->driver_data->wait_for_hdr_fifo &&
-		    samsung_dsim_wait_for_hdr_fifo(dsi))
-			dev_warn(dsi->dev,
-				 "header FIFO not empty before reprogramming\n");
-		samsung_dsim_set_display_enable(dsi, false);
+	if (dsi->plat_data->hw_type != DSIM_TYPE_EXYNOS7870) {
+		samsung_dsim_set_display_mode(dsi);
+		samsung_dsim_set_display_enable(dsi, true);
 	}
 
-	samsung_dsim_set_display_mode(dsi);
-	samsung_dsim_set_display_enable(dsi, true);
-
 	dsi->state |= DSIM_STATE_VIDOUT_AVAILABLE;}
 
 static void samsung_dsim_atomic_disable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
-- 
2.47.3

